  {
   "level": "FAIL",
   "id": "focal-point",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "The first screen has no dominant element: the largest type is 64px (4.4vw) and no single picture holds a third of the viewport.",
   "fix": "Make one thing lead: the headline at display size, or one large picture. A grid of many small pictures is not one thing; in blind tests jurors marked a first screen without a headline down every time. On the strongest studied sites the largest type has a median of 8.4vw."
  },
  {
   "level": "FAIL",
   "id": "off-centre",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "The page sits off-centre: its content comes to 82px from the left edge but only to 393px from the right, at 1440px.",
   "fix": "Give the page one pair of equal margins. Check the wrapper for a max-width without margin-inline: auto, a grid with an empty last column, or padding on one side only. If one side is meant to hold air, it must still be closed by something that reaches the margin (a picture, the navigation's last item, a figure).",
   "alsoAt": [
    768
   ]
  },
  {
   "level": "FAIL",
   "id": "still-page",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "Only 0 element(s) moved while the page loaded and scrolled.",
   "fix": "Build the motion layer (SKILL.md step 9, references/motion.md): the signature move, an entrance for the parts of every section, feedback on every control, and one moving picture. Transform and opacity only, with a reduced-motion fallback."
  },
  {
   "level": "FAIL",
   "id": "empty-screens",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "8 of 12 desktop screens are almost empty ground (under 20% of the screen holds text, a picture or a colour field): screens 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 12.",
   "fix": "An empty screen is a rest only once per page. Elsewhere it means the section is underbuilt: set its content larger, give it the full information, put it on a colour field, or cut it."
  },
  {
   "level": "FAIL",
   "id": "eyebrow",
   "width": 768,
   "message": "1 eyebrow/kicker label(s) above headings: \"Contents\" above \"Changelog\"",
   "fix": "Delete them. If the label carried real information, fold it into the headline or the supporting sentence."
  },
  {
   "level": "WARN",
   "id": "name-only-title",
   "width": 768,
   "message": "The h1 is a bare name (\"Changelog\") and nothing else on the first screen says what this is.",
   "fix": "Keep the name if it leads, and give the line under it (18px or more) the plain words: what it is, for whom, where or when. In the study of 97 Sites of the Day, first screens that named nothing lost usability and content points.",
